In the late afternoon I sit on the sofa with my phone.
I am making my weekly video call with my family in Mexico.
My parents and my little sister Sofia are on the screen.
I turn the camera to Bruno.
I want to show him to my parents and Sofia.
The small dog is lying in his basket and sleeping deeply.
Sofia sees him and smiles.
"Oh, he is so cute!" she calls out happily.
"Wake him up, Maya!" my sister asks.
"I want to see him play."
I quietly shake my head.
"No, I am not allowed to wake him," I explain to her.
"We played for a long time this morning and he is very tired."
"He must rest now."
My mother immediately agrees with me.
"Exactly, let him sleep, Sofia," Mom says.
At this moment, Bruno sighs loudly in his sleep.
My family laughs affectionately.
I turn the camera back to my face and we continue talking.
